<% content_for :javascripts do %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag "api_docs", defer: true %>
<% end %>

<p class="home-lead">
  A free JSON API with dog breeds, breed groups and facts. No key, no sign up,
  no limits worth worrying about — built to be the API you learn on.
</p>

<% if @fact %>
  <blockquote class="home-fact">
    <%= @fact.body %>
    <cite>a random fact, served by this API when the page loaded</cite>
  </blockquote>
<% end %>

<p class="home-actions">
  <%= link_to "Read the docs", docs_path, class: "api-button home-cta" %>
  <%= link_to "Try every endpoint", demo_path, class: "api-button api-button-quiet home-cta" %>
</p>

<h2 id="start">
  <a class="api-anchor" href="#start" aria-hidden="true"></a>
  Start in one request
</h2>

<p>
  Nothing to install and nothing to configure. Paste this in a terminal, or run
  the same thing right here.
</p>

<%= render "pages/api_code",
      label: "Terminal",
      language: "shell",
      id: "home-curl",
      content: 'curl -s "https://dogapi.dog/api/v2/facts?limit=1"' %>

<form class="api-try" data-api-try data-base="/api/v2" data-path="/facts">
  <fieldset>
    <legend>Try it</legend>

    <div class="api-try-fields">
      <div class="api-try-field">
        <label for="home-limit">limit</label>
        <input type="text" id="home-limit" data-param="limit" data-in="query"
               data-default="1" value="1" placeholder="1-5">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="api-try-actions">
      <button type="submit" class="api-button">Send request</button>
      <button type="button" class="api-button api-button-quiet" data-api-reset>Reset</button>
      <span class="api-muted">Runs against this site.</span>
    </div>
  </fieldset>

  <div class="api-try-output" data-api-output hidden>
    <figure class="code">
      <figcaption class="code-head">
        <span class="api-status" data-api-status></span>
        <code class="api-try-url" data-api-url></code>
      </figcaption>
      <pre class="code-body code-body-tall"><code data-api-body></code></pre>
    </figure>
  </div>
</form>

<h2 id="inside">
  <a class="api-anchor" href="#inside" aria-hidden="true"></a>
  What's inside
</h2>

<dl class="home-stats">
  <div>
    <dt><%= number_with_delimiter @counts[:breeds] %></dt>
    <dd>breeds, each with life span, weight ranges and a description</dd>
  </div>
  <div>
    <dt><%= number_with_delimiter @counts[:groups] %></dt>
    <dd>breed groups, linked to the breeds they contain</dd>
  </div>
  <div>
    <dt><%= number_with_delimiter @counts[:facts] %></dt>
    <dd>dog facts, served at random</dd>
  </div>
</dl>

<h2 id="teaching">
  <a class="api-anchor" href="#teaching" aria-hidden="true"></a>
  Made for classrooms and side projects
</h2>

<p>
  This API is used by universities, bootcamps, home labs and a lot of people
  learning to code. That shapes what it does and what it refuses to do.
</p>

<ul class="home-points">
  <li>
    <strong>No key, no account.</strong> Nothing to sign up for and nothing to
    leak in a public repository or a screen share.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Works from the browser.</strong> CORS is open for reads, so
    <code>fetch()</code> works from a static page, CodePen or a classroom laptop
    with no proxy in between.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Small, predictable payloads.</strong> V2 follows JSON:API, so once
    a student can read one response they can read all of them.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Kind to slow connections.</strong> Responses are a few kilobytes,
    served over HTTPS, cached at the edge where it is safe to do so.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Fair use, not a quota.</strong> 300 requests per minute per IP is
    plenty for a full classroom. There is no monthly limit to run out of
    mid-lesson.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Stable.</strong> V1 has been answering since 2016 and still does.
    V2 is the one to build on.
  </li>
</ul>

<h3 id="exercises">
  <a class="api-anchor" href="#exercises" aria-hidden="true"></a>
  Ideas to teach with
</h3>

<p>Each of these needs no backend, no key and no setup beyond a text editor:</p>

<ul class="home-points">
  <li>
    <strong>First fetch.</strong> Show one random fact on a page, then a button
    that swaps it for another.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Lists and loops.</strong> Render every breed with
    <code>?page[size]=1000</code>, then add a search box that filters client
    side.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Pagination.</strong> Walk pages with <code>page[number]</code> and
    read the totals out of <code>meta.pagination</code>.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Relationships.</strong> Pick a group, follow
    <code>relationships.breeds</code>, and fetch each breed by id.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Handling errors.</strong> Request a breed id that does not exist and
    handle the 404 without breaking the page.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Charts.</strong> Plot life span or weight ranges across a group and
    talk about what the numbers do and do not say.
  </li>
</ul>

<p>
  Built something with it? Send it to
  <%= mail_to "dev@dogapi.dog" %> — seeing what people make is what keeps this
  running.
</p>

