<h2 id="faq">
  <a class="api-anchor" href="#faq" aria-hidden="true"></a>
  Questions
</h2>

<h3>Do I need an API key?</h3>
<p>
  No, and there is no plan to require one. If that ever changes, existing
  requests will keep working.
</p>

<h3>Why is it free?</h3>
<p>
  It is used as a teaching tool and for fun, and it has been hosted for free for
  years. Keeping it that way matters more than making money from it. If you want
  to help with the hosting bill, you can
  <%= link_to "buy me a coffee", "https://www.buymeacoffee.com/kinduff", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>.
</p>

<h3>Can I use it in a course, a workshop or a tutorial?</h3>
<p>
  Yes, including commercial courses, with no need to ask. A link back is
  appreciated but not required. If you are teaching a large group, nothing
  special is needed — the rate limit is per IP, and a classroom behind one
  address is well within it.
</p>

<h3>Why is V1 deprecated?</h3>
<p>
  V1 does not follow any standard and was not built to grow. V2 follows JSON:API
  and is where breeds, groups and everything new lives. V1 still answers, and
  will keep answering.
</p>

<h3>Where's the Slack button?</h3>
<p>
  Ownership of the Slack application was lost to a policy change and could not
  be recovered.
</p>

<h3>Who makes this?</h3>
<p>
  <%= link_to "kinduff", "https://kinduff.com", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>,
  who likes building silly things and sharing them. The code is
  <%= link_to "on GitHub", "https://github.com/kinduff/dogapi.dog", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>
  under the MIT license.
</p>

